{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"agent_message","text":"**VERDICT: no_break_found.** No concrete remaining evidence-loss mechanism introduced by this correction was found within the examined scope.\n\nI verified eight inspected source files byte-for-byte against tree `a9808f2f6216788eb0dcb67ae5a4791aeba6e2c1`, and examined relevant differences against base `e9faed6357b999774e3bfaae85ac43eff18c9262`. Citations below are snapshot-relative under `trai_brain/mercury-bridge/`.\n\n- **The missing/null-response counterexample is fixed.** `codex-challenger.js:53-61` includes the malformed completion in observations, records `invalid_provider_completion`, and prevents empty-observation identity verification. Line 157 safely produces a null verdict-model entry. Lines 98-99 extract “Actual review answer”; lines 169-177 attach both captured tapes and return that answer.\n- **Both consumers retain the evidence.** Preflight persists stdout/stderr at `provider-preflight.js:143-161,189`, then derives `ok` and receipt status from the same termination classification at lines 190-204. The stage persists both tapes at `adversarial-review.js:1121-1125`, returns the answer at lines 1137-1138, and preserves it in the review result at lines 1244-1259. Identity quarantine does not discard it. The actual persistence callback is wired at `ask.js:960-965,1319-1321`; `run-ledger.js:51-72` writes and hashes the supplied buffers.\n- **Malformed namespace traversal no longer recurses.** `codex-challenger.js:68-86` uses an explicit stack and records malformed-entry diagnostics. Exclusion from parsed catalogs does not remove content from the raw tapes.\n\n**I withdraw the claimed active Astra consumer through `classifyFableFallbackError`.** The production-source search found its definition and export, but no caller. Astra dispatch directly invokes `executePromptOnlyStage` at `adversarial-review.js:1220-1242`; preflight directly checks Astra at `provider-preflight.js:244-250`. Furthermore, supplied Astra identity posture returns immediately at `adversarial-review.js:920-923`; Claude alias matching is restricted to Claude provenance at lines 938-941.\n\nTwo qualifications to Mercury’s testimony:\n\n- “Never throws” and “always records” exceed this static evidence. Existing persistence failures and consumer fallback paths remain; I found no newly introduced trigger here.\n- Non-null malformed model values are **not universally normalized to null**: line 157 uses `?? null`. They receive diagnostics and remain in evidence. That discrepancy does not establish evidence loss.\n\nCoverage: parser, metadata construction, namespace traversal, client factory, preflight/stage consumers, raw writer, identity/fallback routing, and relevant base/prior-correction differences. Existing consumer fallback behavior is distinct from the repaired adapter dereference. No tests, provider calls, mutations, or runtime changes were performed; the reported 57 host tests were not independently verified."}}
